        "body": "Component 4 agreement (#172): agreed.\r\n\r\nAbsence of an application import is not evidence that a dependency is unused,\r\nbecause another dependency can call it. no_usage_detected now needs an\r\nobserved import with no matching call on a closed candidate set, an\r\nunimported occurrence alone gives unknown / insufficient_information. Matched\r\npositive evidence still gives usage_detected. This matches Component 4's rule\r\nthat incomplete evidence cannot produce a negative.\r\n\r\nChecked at 987d50a:\r\n- internal/decision and internal/audit tests pass; go vet and golangci-lint\r\n  clean.\r\n- DetermineState applies the check after positive evidence and adds one\r\n  justification reason (5d); the wording is lint-clean.\r\n- validate.py's occurrence-or-purl match mirrors findingScope.tied(); purl is\r\n  required on findings.\r\n- The three real S5-14 audit cases (#124) give the same decisions on main and\r\n  on this PR (0 no_usage_detected in 93 findings), so S6-10/S6-11 inputs are\r\n  unaffected.\r\n\r\nFollow-up on my side: S6-10 (#157) and S6-12 (#159) will describe the\r\n\"no direct usage evidence\" section as imported-but-not-called only.\r\n\r\nZane (Component 4), 25 October 2026",
        "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
